docs/CROSS-LLM-THREAT-MODEL.md:349:1. **`.claude/governance/codex-cli-pin-manifest.json`** ✅ **SHIPPED ADR-182** — per-targetTriple SHA-256 pin of the NATIVE Codex payload (`payloads.<triple>.{path,sha256}`) plus npm `dist.integrity` provenance for the platform package. This replaces `.claude/governance/codex-cli-binary-sha256.txt`, which is retired as a comment-only tombstone: its `shasum -a 256 $(which codex)` procedure hashed the npm JS launcher, not the executing payload (see Vulnerability (b) above). Pin update ceremony (ADR-182 §Ceremony): after a legitimate upgrade the Owner runs `python3 .claude/hooks/check_pair_rail.py --verify-codex-pin`, transcribes the reported payload `sha256` + `target_triple` into the manifest together with the registry `dist.integrity`, and lands the edit sentinel-gated (the manifest is canonical-guarded under `.claude/governance/*.json` AND kernel-enrolled in `_KERNEL_PATHS`).
docs/CROSS-LLM-THREAT-MODEL.md:352:4. **`check_pair_rail.py` verify-then-invoke at EVERY Codex invocation** ✅ **SHIPPED ADR-182** (supersedes the former `codex.py` TOCTOU-heuristic intent) — `_resolve_codex_bin()` mirrors the launcher's `findCodexExecutable()` to resolve the native payload, computes its SHA-256, compares against the manifest entry, and returns the verified absolute path; `_invoke_codex_review()` execs EXACTLY that path (never `codex` re-resolved from `$PATH`, never the launcher). Mismatch / triple-absent → fail-CLOSED `{decision: block}` (`pair_rail_codex_pin_mismatch` audit); manifest-unreadable / payload-missing → INFRA fail-OPEN advisory per the hook's standing doctrine. This closes the PATH-decoy, package-upgrade, and launcher-indirection arms of T-8 at the call site, and narrows the symlink-pivot TOCTOU to the hash→exec window on one already-resolved absolute path.
