   630	- `.claude/pitfalls-catalog.yaml`, `.claude/task-chains.yaml`
   631	- `PROTOCOL.md` pointer (skipped on `--ceremony user` installs — a user
   632	  install never creates root files)
   633	- `SPEC/v1/` — **forced route** (skipped on `--ceremony user` installs):
   634	  the SPEC is the published compliance contract, so a local edit is a
   635	  *fork of the contract*, not a customization — a framework-owned
   636	  `SPEC/v1` is backed up to `.claude.bak/<timestamp>/SPEC/v1` and
   637	  replaced wholesale. Ownership follows the recorded delivery (the
   638	  ADR-155 baseline manifest); a pre-existing `SPEC/v1` with no delivery
   639	  record is byte-compared against the pristine SPECs shipped at v1.2.0
   640	  and earlier — a match refreshes it, anything else is preserved in
   641	  place with a named WARNING (ADR-155-AMEND-1).
   642	- `.claude/.framework-version` — the framework version marker, rewritten
   643	  to the source version on every upgrade (this is what
   644	  `check-framework-updates.sh` and forensic triage read post-upgrade).
   645	
   646	What is **NOT** touched (user data):
   647	
   648	- `CLAUDE.md`, `MEMORY.md`
   649	- `.claude/agent-metrics.md`
   650	- `VERSION` (root) — **deliberately**: `install.sh` is skip-if-exists,
   651	  so on an adopter repo with its own `VERSION` the framework never
   652	  wrote there, and an upgrade overwrite would take the adopter's file
   653	  (the S238/ADR-155 class). The root `VERSION` is an install-time
   654	  snapshot forever; the current framework version lives in
   655	  `.claude/.framework-version`. Do not "fix" this asymmetry — see
   656	  `ADR-155-AMEND-1`.
   657	
   658	Ceremony on upgrade: `upgrade.sh` reads the recorded install ceremony
   659	from `.claude/.install-state.json` with a dedicated reader that runs
   660	even under `--no-replay`. **Installs without a readable
   661	`.install-state.json` (all pre-Wave-B installs) are treated as
   662	`maintainer` on upgrade** — that is the fail-open, pre-existing
   663	behavior; if your install was `--ceremony user` and predates the state
   664	file, re-run `install.sh --ceremony user` once so the ceremony is
   665	recorded before upgrading.
   666	
   667	`.claude/settings.json` is a special case since v1.2.0: `upgrade.sh` runs a
   668	3-state per-leaf-key **baseline migration** on it (e.g. the pair-rail
   669	registration-timeout cap 150 → 210 s, ADR-110-AMEND-2). A key is only
   670	changed when it still holds the old framework default — operator-chosen
   671	values are preserved — and the pre-migration file is copied to
   672	`.claude.bak/<timestamp>/` first.
   673	
   674	Run `bash scripts/upgrade.sh --help` for the full flag list. Key
   675	flags:
   676	
   677	- `--pin <tag>` — pin source to a specific tag/SHA (refuses if
   678	  target has uncommitted `.claude/` changes; the pin is the audit
   679	  anchor for what was actually installed).
   680	- `--dry-run` — preview what WOULD be replaced.
   681	- `--skip <glob>` — exclude files from the overwrite (repeatable).
   682	  Use this to protect adopter customizations to specific framework
   683	  scripts (e.g. `--skip='.claude/scripts/local/*'`).
   684	- `--no-diff-warn` — silence the F-CHAOS-3 "customization will be
   685	  replaced" warnings (default: warnings ON).
   686	
