   **FILE:LINE:** [scripts/upgrade.sh:766](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.rYItrR/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:766), [scripts/upgrade.sh:3156](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.rYItrR/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:3156)

   **Failure scenario:** When historical install-state is absent, upgrade defaults the effective ceremony to maintainer and writes root `.gitignore` blocks. A pre-state user-only installation can therefore receive root writes despite the user-ceremony boundary. The efficacy test begins at the v1.2.0 pin and does not cover this population.

   **Minimal fix:** Add an explicit ceremony override or require positive maintainer evidence before root delivery, then cover a pre-install-state user fixture.

