Concrete failure scenario: this is valid YAML:

```yaml
verdict: GO
  NO-GO
release_tag: v1.3.0-rc.4
```

Both PyYAML and Ruby YAML resolve `verdict` as the non-authorizing scalar `GO NO-GO`. Both new shape gates, however, unconditionally ignore indented lines; both minimal parsers therefore see exactly `GO`. With an otherwise-valid envelope/delta, direct full-path probes returned server `0` and local guard `0`.

The regression suite compares the two readers to each other, so this both-wrong interpretation passes its parity control. This violates the advertised exact-token and fail-closed semantics.

Minimal fix: in both readers, reject any non-comment indented continuation belonging to a scalar `verdict:` declaration. Add this exact fixture to the server workflow-argv and local delta suites, requiring exit 3/E_DECISION. Keep legitimate nested lines under mapping/list fields green.

